# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# ONE clipboard for the desk.  Text selected on an editor's page is
# copied and pasted into ANOTHER editor's page; then into the SHELL'S
# own Save-panel field, where it names the file being made; then a name
# copied out of that field lands back on a page.  Application to
# application, application to shell, shell to application -- one store,
# and out of process every road crosses the wire.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
key Home
wait 3
key Right
key Right
key Right
wait 3
key End shift
wait 6
key c ctrl
wait 8
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
key Down
wait 6
key Return
wait 90
expect-title util.bas
note the page wears an Edit menu, and its Paste is the same paste
click 117 8
wait 8
expect-menu Cut|Copy|Paste|Select all|
menu-pick Paste
wait 8
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/util.bas 40 deltagamma
click-window Project
wait 8
click 132 8
wait 8
menu-pick New File…
wait 40
expect-title Save
key a ctrl
wait 4
key v ctrl
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 90
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/project.tiku file gamma
note and BACK: a name copied out of the shell's own field lands on an
note editor's page, replacing the selection still held there
click-window Project
wait 8
click 132 8
wait 8
menu-pick New File…
wait 40
expect-title Save
key a ctrl
wait 4
key c ctrl
wait 6
click 587 413
wait 30
click-window Project
wait 8
click 185 8
wait 8
menu-pick main.bas
wait 30
expect-title main.bas
key v ctrl
wait 8
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 untitled.bas
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 gamma
quit
